{
  "_doc": "---------------------------------------------------------------- BUILDINGS\nplaces, their staff/role, whether they shelter, and their rooms/affordances.\nCatalogue buildings that are NOT standing when the town is founded (`founding: False`). They\nare valid places -- a trade can name them and a BUILDING_PROJECT can raise them -- but the\nfounding town does not contain them (see founding_buildings()).\nA building may carry one `door` (Phase 039): a lock (lock_id, locked, keys_required, lock_strength, as Phase 030 and 050 use for containers) and an `entrance` cell, an offset [dx, dy] inside the footprint on its perimeter. A step across the footprint boundary is refused while the door is locked; while it is unlocked, a crossing is allowed only at the entrance cell. Founding buildings have no door. The jail's lock_strength 3.0 and lock_id 41 are APPROX (design choices; no source consulted). The jail is locked when it is built or when a scenario adds it. The world attaches no law or sentence to it.",
  "_types": {
